# Sanity Studio — copy to `.env` (same `SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID` as `web/.env.local`)
#
# Hosting: by default the Studio deploys to Netlify on its own domain (`studio/netlify.toml`).
# Set the "Deployment" values below on the Netlify Studio site too. Sanity Hosting
# (`*.sanity.studio`, `pnpm studio:deploy`) stays available — see the last hosting section.
#
# PUBLIC vs SECRET: the Studio build inlines EVERY `SANITY_STUDIO_*` variable into its public
# JS bundle. Never put a token, secret or password under that prefix — `sanity build` /
# `sanity deploy` refuse to run with one set (`sanity.cli.ts`). Secrets below use plain names.

SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=

# --- Deployment: dataset, preview origin, hosting URL ---
#
# Dataset this Studio edits. Empty = auto-select (next section): development first locally
# and on deploy previews, production first on production. On the Netlify Studio site set it
# per deploy context (Production: production; Deploy Previews + Branch deploys: development),
# so the hosted Studio skips its dataset probe at load.
SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=
#
# Web origin Presentation opens — scheme + host + port; localhost:3000 ≠ 127.0.0.1:3000.
# Netlify Studio site: the production web origin, e.g. https://www.your-domain.tld
SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
# More web origins Presentation may load, comma-separated (e.g. web deploy previews).
# SANITY_STUDIO_WEB_PREVIEW_ORIGINS=https://your-site.netlify.app,https://deploy-preview-42--your-site.netlify.app
#
# This Studio's own public URL: the custom domain of the Netlify Studio site. Also:
# - add it in sanity.io/manage → API → CORS origins, **with credentials** (login needs it);
# - set it as `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_STUDIO_URL` in `web/.env.local` and on the web site
#   (CSP `frame-ancestors` for Presentation, click-to-edit links).
# `pnpm studio:register` registers it with Sanity. On Netlify, empty falls back to the
# site's primary domain (`URL`).
SANITY_STUDIO_HOSTING_URL=
#
# Deploy token (sanity.io/manage → API → Tokens) — on the Netlify Studio site only, never
# in a committed file. With it, every production deploy runs `pnpm studio:register`
# (registers the URL, uploads the schema). Locally, `sanity login` does the same job.
# SANITY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# --- Dataset auto-selection (`@repo/sanity-dataset-resolve`, `config/sync/studioDataset.ts`) ---
# Applies while `SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET` is empty. `studio/netlify.toml` already sets the
# target per Netlify deploy context.
#
# Same override as web — set `SANITY_STUDIO_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET` on the **Studio build’s** env
# (e.g. Sanity deploy env vars) to match your staging/preview dataset name (`staging`, etc.).
# SANITY_STUDIO_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=staging
#
# Optional: rename canonical dev/prod labels if your project uses different dataset names.
# SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET_DEVELOPMENT=development
# SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET_PRODUCTION=production
# Dataset sync: `pnpm run sync:prod-to-dev` in `studio/` (or `pnpm studio:sync-prod-to-dev` from repo root).

# --- Optional: dataset-probing token (secret — no `SANITY_STUDIO_` prefix) ---
# Used by `@repo/sanity-dataset-resolve` to enumerate datasets via the Management API
# when `SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET` is not pinned (avoids the public probe fallback). CLI only:
# the Studio in the browser never sees it and probes instead. `SANITY_AUTH_TOKEN` works too.
# Formerly `SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET_RESOLVER_TOKEN` — rename it if you still have it.
# SANITY_DATASET_RESOLVER_TOKEN=
#
# Read token for the one-off migration scripts in `scripts/` (same value as web).
# SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN=

# --- Alternative hosting: Sanity (`*.sanity.studio`, `pnpm studio:deploy`) ---
# App id of this project's Sanity-hosted Studio, so deploys update it without a hostname
# prompt. `sanity deploy` prints it after the first deploy. Per project — don't copy a
# fork's value. Not needed for Netlify; `pnpm studio:register` ignores it.
# SANITY_STUDIO_APP_ID=

# --- Optional: Mux API token (secret — no `SANITY_STUDIO_` prefix) ---
# Only for the one-off `pnpm mux:migrate-assets` (dry-run) / `pnpm mux:migrate-assets -- --apply`.
# The Studio's Mux plugin keeps its own credentials in the dataset (plugin settings), not here.
# Formerly `SANITY_STUDIO_MUX_TOKEN_ID` / `_SECRET` — rename them if you still have them.
# MUX_TOKEN_ID=
# MUX_TOKEN_SECRET=
